# The core function deploys from the repository root so `import src` resolves.
# Everything the function does not read at runtime stays out of the upload.
#
# This is belt; `vercel.json`'s `excludeFiles` is braces. `.vercelignore`
# filters what is *uploaded*, `excludeFiles` filters what goes into the
# function *bundle* — and only the second applies to a local `vercel build`,
# which is how `.env.local` (the Vercel OIDC token) was found sitting in a
# bundle here. Keep the two lists agreeing.
#
# `config/` and `data/` are deliberately NOT here: `cli.load_config` reads the
# first and `run.CHECKOUT_DATA` the second, both out of the deployment.
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT here either: `vercel.json`'s `ignoreCommand` runs
# `git diff HEAD^ HEAD` against the build filesystem, and `.vercelignore` is
# applied before that command runs. Stripping `.git` here made every deploy
# since d325890 fail with "Not a git repository". `excludeFiles` on each
# function still keeps `.git/**` out of the deployed bundle.
.github
.claude
.venv
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.env
.env.local
tests
ci
ops
db
docs
services/core/tests
uv.lock
README.md
